config LOG
	bool "log: loggers, log sinks, and printf-style call sites"
	default y
	select STATUS
	select IO
	select FMT
	select TIME
	help
	  Logging for applications: a logger with a level, a tag, and a clock;
	  the el_log_sink interface that decides where records go; a sink
	  that writes text lines to an el_writer, and one that keeps records
	  in caller-provided memory; and the contract test suite for sinks.
	  Elemental's own modules never log.

config LOG_DEFERRED
	bool "log_deferred: a sink that hands records to another context"
	default y
	depends on LOG && RING
	help
	  el_log_deferred_sink: a sink that copies each record into an
	  el_ring and returns, for an interrupt handler or any code that must
	  not wait for where its records are written; another context drains
	  the ring into the sink that writes. It is the one part of log that
	  needs ring: turn it off and log builds and links no ring.
	  Freestanding: needs memcpy().
